AB  - Readers respond to Alan Milburn's recommendation that primary schools may be able to spot children at risk of future unemployment Alan Milburn suggests that primary schools should be asked to spot children at risk of future unemployment ( Primary schools to be told to identify children at risk of future unemployment, 7 August ). Intervening early makes sense. Children who miss a lot of school do tend to drift away from it later, and waiting until someone is 18 and out of work is obviously too late. But there is a difference between spotting what a child needs and deciding what they will…
